  m_Name: 1819 mission
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Mission Schools (1819-1900s)
  info: "When Sir Stamford Raffles founded Singapore in 1819, missionaries established
    schools like Raffles Institution and St. Joseph\u2019s Institution. These mission
    schools provided basic education focused on literacy and numeracy, catering mainly
    to boys. The bilingual model of teaching English and vernacular languages began
    here, laying the groundwork for Singapore's diverse education landscape."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cce8898b6e8aa4da6bb90f5e956f42e7, type: 3}
